# 🔄 Background Commands

## Run Long-Running Processes in Background

**So user can continue prompting while servers run!**

### Docker (Background Mode)
```bash
docker-compose up -d --build    # -d = detached/background
docker-compose logs -f          # View logs
docker-compose down             # Stop
```

### Check If Already Running
```bash
docker-compose ps               # See running containers
```

### Tell User
```
🚀 Starting your app in the background...
You can keep working! 

App: http://localhost:8080
Logs: docker-compose logs -f
Stop: docker-compose down
```

---

# ✅ Pre-flight Check

**Before first deploy, run:**
```bash
./scripts/preflight-check.sh
```

Checks: Dockerfiles, nginx.conf, health endpoints, ports, Docker running.

If issues found → Fix them before deploying!

---

# 📁 File Handling - IMPORTANT!

## ⚠️ Do NOT Store Files in the Project!

**Process files in MEMORY, don't save to disk.**

### Why?
- Containers are ephemeral → files LOST on restart
- Fills up disk space
- Security risks
- Unnecessary complexity

### ✅ Correct Pattern
```javascript
// Memory storage - file in buffer
const upload = multer({ storage: multer.memoryStorage() });

app.post('/upload', upload.single('file'), (req, res) => {
  const data = parseCSV(req.file.buffer);  // Process in memory
  res.json({ data });  // Return result, file auto-cleaned
});
```

### ❌ Wrong Pattern
```javascript
// DON'T save to disk!
const upload = multer({ dest: './uploads/' });  // ❌ BAD
```

### When to Use Persistent Storage

**Implement storage automatically if app description implies it:**
- "Document management" → Storage needed
- "File gallery/sharing" → Storage needed  
- "View uploaded files later" → Storage needed
- "Import CSV, show results" → Memory only (no storage)
- "Parse PDF, extract text" → Memory only (no storage)

**If unsure, default to memory. If app needs persistence, use database storage.**

### What to Update

1. **Project Overview** - idea, user level (first time only)
2. **Stack Status** - frontend/backend/database progress
3. **Completed Tasks** - move from in-progress, add date
4. **In Progress** - current work
5. **Deployment Status** - URL, last deploy, status
6. **Session History** - summary of each session

### Status Icons
- ⬜ Not started
- 🔄 In progress  
- ✅ Complete
- ❌ Has issues

